See-through textures keep their one level: a one level texture given a chain (0006, 0008) that has any alpha below
solid (foliage, fences, wire) is drawn from its top level alone, as the console drew it. Its averaged levels thinned
its alpha whatever the game's test or blend, and plants faded away within a few steps; matching the levels' alpha to
the top's did not hold either. Opaque textures keep their chain.

diff --git a/runtime/gpu/d3d12.cpp b/runtime/gpu/d3d12.cpp
index 306ef0e..d07bbac 100644
